<title>USA: Faulding gets FDA approval for acyclovir.</title>
<headline>Faulding gets FDA approval for acyclovir.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETH, N.J. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Faulding Inc said Tuesday that its Faulding Pharmaceutical Co subsidiary got final approval from the Food and Drug Administration to market acyclovir injection, the generic version of Zovirax brand of acyclovir sodium sterile powder.</p>
<p>Zovirax is manufactured by Glaxo Wellcome Plc.</p>
<p>The injection contains acyclovir, an antiviral drug active against herpes viruses, the company said.</p>
<p>Faulding said it plans a prompt commercial launch.</p>
</text>
